<BaseLayout title="About" description="Background on SLP/IO, Harmonic Systems, and the clinician-developer behind the project.">
    <section>
        <div class="section-header">
            <div class="section-label">Background</div>
            <h2>About <span class="accent">This Resource</span></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>Built by a clinician, for clinicians. SLP/IO is a <strong>Harmonic Systems</strong> project — a speech-language pathologist and software developer who has spent years writing the same IEP goals, progress notes, and evaluation reports that you write.</p>

            <p>This resource is free, not affiliated with any vendor or institution, and oriented toward sharpening clinical judgment rather than replacing it. LLM-assisted clinical writing is real work that deserves real craft — not a shortcut, but a skill that requires both clinical judgment and the ability to read what a model produces.</p>

            <p>The knowledge inside this guide isn't new. It's what competent clinicians already know: assessment frameworks, legal standards, clinical reasoning, ethical boundaries. We organized it in a way that makes it usable with modern tools and readable with a critical eye. Clinicians deserve to participate in how their paperwork evolves, not have it decided for them.</p>

            <blockquote>
                <strong>About Harmonic Systems:</strong> A small, independent studio in the Hudson Valley region of New York, built by a school-based speech-language pathologist who also writes software. SLP/IO is an attempt to bridge the gap between what clinicians need and what the technology conversation currently offers.
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Contact</h3>
